  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Citizen Engagement Activity</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(Kosovo):  .Kosovo&apos;s civil society has made significant progress over the last 20 years, largely with USAID assistance. However, gaps in the capacity and accountability of local civil society organizations (CSOs) and public institutions, as well as low social trust, hamper the ability of civil society to be an effective bridge between the citizens and their government. With FY22 funds, the Citizen Engagement Activity will work with Kosovo&apos;s civil society to embrace new approaches to working with their constituencies, to adopt a more strategic perspective on both intra and inter-sectoral partnerships, and to diversify its resource and partner base. Specifically, the activity will foster connections between youth activists and CSOs, build CSO community mobilization and fundraising skills, improve the legal environment and develop tech solutions for civil society&apos;s financial transparency and for individual and corporate philanthropy, support implementation of Government-Civil society cooperation strategy, and promote skilled volunteerism. The activity aligns with ICS objective 2.2: Institutions&apos; transparency and ability to respond to all citizens&apos; needs; deliver quality services; implement laws, regulations, and court decisions; and reduce corruption is enhanced and with JRS Goal 3.1: Promote good governance and defend strong, accountable, and resilient democracies that deliver for their citizens. This activity also aligns with CAATSA #5 by strengthening the capacity of CSOs to represent citizens&apos; interests, which in turn will contribute to a constructive environment for Kosovo&apos;s development and prosperity. This activity contributes to the following directives and key issues: democracy directive and women, peace and security... .</narrative>
  </description>
